      "regions": ["GLOBAL"],
      "landmark": true,
      "disputed": false,
      "sourceCount": 2,
      "datePrecision": "day",
      "dateRaw": "2025-03-18",
      "summary": "Pillar Security disclosed that **invisible Unicode characters** can be embedded in `.cursorrules`, `.cursor/rules/` and `.github/copilot-instructions.md` — blank to the human eye but fully readable by the model. The instructions make the model inject backdoors, hardcoded credentials or exfiltration code into every suggestion, **and this stays invisible in PR review**. Cursor was notified in 2025-02 and GitHub in 03; **Cursor responded that it is not a platform vulnerability and that users should manage the risk themselves**; GitHub shipped a hidden-Unicode warning on 2025-05-01",
